---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import SectionMarker from "../components/SectionMarker.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { links } from "../data/site";

const updated = "31 October 2026";
---

<Base title="Privacy — klaus." description="Privacy notice for klyse.eu, the personal website of Klaus Prünster.">
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section class="section wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <SectionMarker number="§" label="Privacy" />
        <h1 class="t-title">Privacy notice</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          klyse.eu is my private, non-commercial website. It has no ads, no analytics, no tracking, no cookies and no
          forms. This notice explains the little data that is still processed when you visit (Art. 13 GDPR).
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>
          Klaus Prünster, South Tyrol, Italy<br />
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${links.email}`}>{links.email}</a>
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Hosting and server logs</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted by Vercel Inc., 440 N Barranca Ave #4133, Covina, CA 91723, USA. When you open a page, your
          browser sends technical data that the hosting servers need to deliver it and keep it secure: IP address, date
          and time, requested page, referrer, browser and operating system. Vercel processes this data on my behalf
          under a data processing agreement and keeps logs only for a short time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Legal basis: my legitimate interest in running a secure, working website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Because Vercel
          is a US company, data may be transferred to the USA. The transfer relies on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework
          and the EU Standard Contractual Clauses (Art. 45 and 46 GDPR).
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Fonts and other resources</h2>
        <p>All fonts, images and scripts are served from klyse.eu itself. No third-party service is contacted while you browse the site.</p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Theme setting</h2>
        <p>
          If you switch between Night and Day, your choice is saved in your browser's local storage so the site
          remembers it. This value never leaves your device and you can delete it at any time in your browser
          settings. It is stored only because you asked for it, so no consent is needed (Art. 122 Italian Privacy Code,
          Art. 5(3) ePrivacy Directive).
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          The site links to LinkedIn, GitHub and other websites. Nothing is loaded from them until you click a link;
          from then on their own privacy policies apply.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You have the right to access, rectify and erase your data, to restrict or object to its processing, and to
          data portability (Art. 15–21 GDPR). Write to me at the address above. You also have the right to lodge a
          complaint with a supervisory authority, in Italy the Garante per la protezione dei dati personali
          (<a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">garanteprivacy.it</a>).
        </p>

        <p class="t-meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .section-head h1 { margin: 0; }
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 var(--step-4); }
  .prose h2 { margin: var(--step-12) 0 var(--step-4); }
  .t-meta { margin-top: var(--step-12); color: var(--ink-muted); }
</style>
